From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: youss17x <a.fzc17@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 140/140] PC5: a page decommitted beside an inaccessible one is
 cleared with its host page open, so NW.js games (Fear & Hunger) don't stop at
 start (Wine patch 1008)

---
 ...ommitted-page-beside-a-protected-one.patch | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1008-ntdll-clear-a-decommitted-page-beside-a-protected-one.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1008-ntdll-clear-a-decommitted-page-beside-a-protected-one.patch b/wine/patches/1008-ntdll-clear-a-decommitted-page-beside-a-protected-one.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..269d5ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1008-ntdll-clear-a-decommitted-page-beside-a-protected-one.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: youss17x <a.fzc17@gmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Clear a decommitted page beside a protected one with
+ its host page open.
+
+Patch 0893 clears the decommitted pages of a host page that keeps other
+pages committed, after making each one writable with mprotect_range().
+Since 0974, a committed read-only or inaccessible page takes writing, or
+all access, away from its whole host page, so a page beside one stayed
+closed and memset() faulted inside NtFreeVirtualMemory, where
+virtual_handle_fault cannot step over it: the call failed with
+STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION.
+
+Chromium's PartitionAlloc decommits pages beside inaccessible guard pages
+all the time and treats a failed decommit as fatal. NW.js games (RPG Maker
+MV, Fear & Hunger with --single-process) stopped on a breakpoint in nw.dll
+three seconds after starting: "Check failed:
+SetSystemPagesAccess(address, length, PageInaccessible)".
+
+The host page is now opened whole, keeping what its pages already allowed,
+for the clearing; decommit_pages() already gives every partial host page
+the protection its remaining pages need afterwards.
+---
+ dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 13 +++++++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+index 7d1212d..58cf986 100644
+--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
++++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+@@ -3062,12 +3062,21 @@ static SIZE_T get_committed_size( struct file_view *view, void *base, size_t max
+  */
+ static NTSTATUS clear_committed_pages( char *start, char *end )
+ {
+-    char *page;
++    char *page, *host_page;
++    int prot;
+ 
+     for (page = start; page < end; page += page_size)
+     {
+         if (!(get_page_vprot( page ) & VPROT_COMMITTED)) continue;
+-        if (mprotect_range( page, page_size, VPROT_READ | VPROT_WRITE, VPROT_GUARD | VPROT_WRITEWATCH ))
++        /* Open the whole host page. mprotect_range() would keep it closed when a
++         * committed page beside this one is read-only or inaccessible (0974), and
++         * memset() would then fault here, in the syscall, where virtual_handle_fault
++         * cannot step over it. decommit_pages() gives the host page its protection
++         * back once the pages are cleared. */
++        host_page = ROUND_ADDR( page, host_page_mask );
++        prot = get_unix_prot( get_host_page_vprot( page ) & ~(VPROT_GUARD | VPROT_WRITEWATCH) );
++        if (mprotect_exec( host_page, host_page_size, prot | PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE ) &&
++            mprotect( host_page, host_page_size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE ))
+             return STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED;
+         memset( page, 0, page_size );
+     }
-- 
